From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 15:36:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] flow: the .odb carries its timing constraints
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Builds on "restore timing constraints from the .odb when it carries them"
and retires the fallback: every .odb now stores the constraints it was
written with (OpenROAD write_db) and load_design restores them with
read_db -sdc, so the flow no longer carries a matching .sdc next to every
.odb and no longer has to work out which .sdc goes with which .odb.

read_sdc and write_sdc stay what they are good at: the human interface.
The design's SDC_FILE is parsed exactly once, at synthesis, where
OpenSTA's forgiving reader is a feature. From there the constraints
ride in the .odb, compact and never out of sync with the design.

What goes:
- find_sdc_file (util.tcl): the glob of results/, the dictionary sort
  and "greatest .sdc at or below this .odb's stem" guess, and its two
  callers in open.tcl and generate_abstract.tcl.
- load_design's sdc argument for .odb inputs; the Verilog path keeps it
  (synthesis reads the design's SDC).
- The intermediate .sdc files (2_1_floorplan, 2_floorplan, 3_place,
  4_cts, 5_1_grt, 5_route, 6_1_fill): their write_sdc calls in the stage
  scripts and flow.tcl, and their Makefile targets, copies and
  dependencies.

What stays: 1_synth.sdc (the canonicalized constraints, for inspection
and for genMetrics' clock metrics) and 6_final.sdc (the final export, for
humans and standalone OpenSTA reproductions).

The flow read the .sdc 16 times and wrote it 6 times per run; for a
large design each read_sdc is tens of seconds (the platform constraints
name every register clock pin in every set_max_delay and group_path).
read_db -sdc restores the same constraints in a fraction of that.

Requires an OpenROAD with read_db -sdc (write_db storing constraints).


Carried in bazel-orfs, not upstreamed: the second of two steps, on top
of 0050-orfs-sdc-in-odb-compat.patch. It depends on the OpenROAD patch
that stores constraints in the .odb (OpenROAD PR #11260), carried on the
openroad archive_override in MODULE.bazel. Retires on the //:bump onto an
ORFS that carries this change.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
